  "unable": {
    "evidence_refs": [
      "packages/svelte/src/compiler/phases/3-transform/client/visitors/ConstTag.js:30-36 (create_derived wraps await-containing init in a non-async thunk; baseline compiled output shows invalid `$.derived(() => await Promise.resolve(5))`)",
      "baseline failure: `await isn't allowed in non-async function` in async-are-public-holdout dom+hydrate (public-holdout-v1)",
      "packages/svelte/src/compiler/phases/3-transform/client/utils.js:1-60 (create_derived has no async/await-aware path used by ConstTag)",
      "workflow state: no staging/patch-submission tool is available; candidates list empty and final turn reached"
    ],
    "reason": "Diagnosis is confident but no patch could be staged/submitted: no staging tool is exposed in this environment, so I cannot produce a validated public-green candidate. Root cause: ConstTag.js builds `create_derived(context.state, b.thunk(init))` for `{@const x = await ...}`. When the init contains an AwaitExpression, the emitted thunk arrow is not async, so the client output becomes `$.derived(() => await Promise.resolve(5))` — a non-async function containing await — which fails at parse time ('await isn't allowed in non-async function'). The fix (hyp 1/2, unverified) is to make ConstTag detect an await in the init (node.metadata.expression.contains_await) and emit an async derived thunk consistent with how $derived-with-await is compiled, plus matching SSR handling; this was never staged or evaluated, so correctness (including hydrate mode) is unconfirmed."
  },
